{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/866135-how-addicting-is-the-\u200bkiss-of-the-succubus","id":866135,"title":"How addicting is the \"\u200bKiss of the Succubus\" ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-15T14:56:21-07:00","id":866135,"title":"How addicting is the \"\u200bKiss of the Succubus\" ?","content":"<br /> How addicting is a Kiss of someone with the &quot;\u200bKiss of the Succubus&quot; merit?<br /> <br /> Is it more like a smoking addicting or like a crack or herion addiction?<br /> <br /> How would you imagine the symptoms of this?<br /> <br /> <br /> Kiss of the Succubus (\u2022)<br /> Prerequisite: Must be Daeva<br /> Effect: All Kindred can evoke lustful, passionate reactions <br /> with a bite. The Daeva\u2019s bite is downright addicting. Her Kiss <br /> causes the Addicted Condition in mortals as well as the Swooning <br /> Condition (for Addicted, see p. 301; for Swooning, see p. 306).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11546-christoph","name":"Christoph+","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T15:22:16-07:00","id":866143,"title":"","content":"Well, look at the addicted condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T15:28:41-07:00","id":866148,"title":"","content":"I know, but what does this mean: <br /> <br /> &quot;Your character is addicted to something, whether drugs, <br /> gambling or other destructive behaviors. Some addictions are <br /> more dangerous than others, but the nature of addiction is <br /> that it slowly takes over your life, impeding functionality. If <br /> you are addicted, you need to indulge your addiction regularly <br /> to keep it under control. &quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11546-christoph","name":"Christoph+","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T15:32:53-07:00","id":866149,"title":"","content":"From the FAQ:<br /> <br /> <b><i><b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">What are the mechanics for a victim affected by Kiss of the Succubus?</span></span></span></b></i></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The victim gains the Addicted Condition. Her craving gets stronger each night, and when she sleeps, she dreams of the vampire with increasing frequency. Stamina + Resolve nights after the Kiss, she begins to suffer the Deprived Condition. Her player can delay the onset of Deprived for one night by spending a Willpower point, but cannot spend Willpower to suppress the Condition once the character has begun to suffer it. She can resolve that Condition by experiencing the bite of the vampire.</i><br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> So, the victim starts feelings it the next day, but it doesn't become real bad until about 4 days without a fix (for a bog-standard 2 stamina 2 resolve character).</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T18:16:17-07:00","id":866199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christoph+</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/866135-how-addicting-is-the-\u200bkiss-of-the-succubus#post866135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How addicting is a Kiss of someone with the &quot;\u200bKiss of the Succubus&quot; merit?<br /> <br /> Is it more like a smoking addicting or like a crack or herion addiction?<br /> <br /> How would you imagine the symptoms of this?<br /> <br /> <br /> Kiss of the Succubus (\u2022)<br /> Prerequisite: Must be Daeva<br /> Effect: All Kindred can evoke lustful, passionate reactions<br /> with a bite. The Daeva\u2019s bite is downright addicting. Her Kiss<br /> causes the Addicted Condition in mortals as well as the Swooning<br /> Condition (for Addicted, see p. 301; for Swooning, see p. 306).</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the characters someone made was a Mehket with this particular condition. I didn't know it was Daeva exclusive. (This is coming from someone that makes Daeva).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11528-dangerus-muyoko-project","name":"Dangerus-Muyoko-Project","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T02:27:38-07:00","id":866324,"title":"","content":"Yes, but are there any ideas or references to literature how this addiction feels like?<br /> <br /> Like &quot;being badly in love&quot;? Or like a severe drug addiction? Or how?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11546-christoph","name":"Christoph+","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T02:31:42-07:00","id":866326,"title":"","content":"It's very addicting. Deprived is pretty nasty. And it starts to happen pretty soon. Your dreams get stronger and stronger. I don't think there is a drug to equate it to, and addictions are different for everyone. Some people need 2 packs of smokes a day, some people can get along with one cigarette just fine. <br /> <br /> Though I would keep or Daeva only. It is their thematic ability. They are suppose to be the tempters, the creatures of desire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T06:20:31-07:00","id":866362,"title":"","content":"Lets put it this way.<br /> <br /> Vitae is one of the most addictive and strongest &quot;drugs&quot; in the entire CofD, on par with the strongest street drugs. Each time you taste it, you could become Persistantly Addicted to it unless you succeed at a roll with a cumulative penalty.<br /> <br /> Kiss of the Succubus inflicts the Addicted Condition immediately. Do not pass Go, do not collect $200. The addictive qualities of the Kiss put vitae to shame, and thus, pretty much all other drugs on the market. Like Swooning, the Addicted Condition becomes Persistant with a dramatic feeding, meaning the addictions pretty much last the same amount of time.<br /> <br /> The only advantage vitae has over Kiss is that its arguable if the Kiss of the Succubus can Addict supernaturals. Some say that, yes, it will addict others if you spend the willpower to inflict Swooning. Others say, no, the merit specifically says mortals. Most tend to fall on the side of no, since Addicting an elder is a bit crazy strong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-16-2016, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T06:47:55-07:00","id":866369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christoph+</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/866135-how-addicting-is-the-\u200bkiss-of-the-succubus?p=866324#post866324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but are there any ideas or references to literature how this addiction feels like?<br /> <br /> Like &quot;being badly in love&quot;? Or like a severe drug addiction? Or how?</div> </div> </div> </div>Look at the above FAQ quote. They're addicted to receiving the Kiss from that vampire. They dream of the vampire every night, and deprived only goes away once they receive the Kiss. So dreams, obsessive need.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T11:56:23-07:00","id":866965,"title":"","content":"They receive two conditions: Swooning and Addicted, potentially Deprived.<br /> <br /> The Swooning part causes puppy love, and on top of that, the Addicted condition causes a psychological need for the vampire's bite - and if they don't get their fix, they get the Deprived condition. Basically, the Deprived condition reduces Stamina, Resolve, and Composure dice-pools by one each, which can be explained in-character by the person feeling physically sore (Stamina), mentally worn out (Resolve), and anxious (Composure). They literally feel worse off without getting fed on by a person they suddenly find very attractive. They <i>need </i>that person to make them feel good and complete. And they know it. I could definitely see a person confusing it all for a really unhealthy fixation on the vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T13:22:47-07:00","id":867772,"title":"","content":"How I would picture this ? A stalking obsessive ex. Now are you scared ? ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T13:40:16-07:00","id":867791,"title":"","content":"Considering that, if a Deava feeds twice from this guy or gal, the Deava falls in love with the mortal as well? I'd call that more of a clingy co-dependant relationship than anything. Now expand that out to the other mortals that the Deava will feed from. Jealous, needy harem of addicts all of which the vampire &quot;loves.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T13:42:07-07:00","id":867792,"title":"","content":"Sounds like an anime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T15:26:14-07:00","id":867860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/866135-how-addicting-is-the-\u200bkiss-of-the-succubus?p=867791#post867791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that, if a Deava feeds twice from this guy or gal, the Deava falls in love with the mortal as well? I'd call that more of a clingy co-dependant relationship than anything. Now expand that out to the other mortals that the Deava will feed from. Jealous, needy harem of addicts all of which the vampire &quot;loves.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, they're at risk of this happening, creating the kind of Carmilla-esque destructive relationship that ends in at least one of the parties dying. Definitely think that's one of those interesting things implicit in Kiss of the Succubus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T03:48:12-07:00","id":936012,"title":"","content":"Interesting, how would a blood bond 3, vitae adiction and an addiction caused by the Kiss of Succubus combined together feel like?<br /> <br /> How would this be perceived by the thrall?<br /> <br /> It would probably make it even harder to think about something else than the regnant ....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11546-christoph","name":"Christoph+","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T05:22:20-07:00","id":936034,"title":"","content":"In real life, addictions are complicated and depend on the individual. We can have multiple, we can have crossover or switching, or more. So, its hard to avoid a &quot;depends on the person in question&quot; answer. <br /> <br /> That said, in general, the Kiss is a metaphor for sex, and vitae addiction is basically the ultimate drug addiction. So, we're looking at being someone that's addicted to sex and drugs, possibly rock and roll, all tied to one person. I think that, ultimately, we're just looking at adding a need for sex in the vampire relationships. Yeah, sex is used for control and inspiring devotion, but its not like the Ven, Nos, Grel, or Meh'ket are without their own forms of controlling. Adoration and love is just the Daeva's stick, as opposed to other methods.<br /> <br /> Its ironic that the Daeva aren't called succubi anymore, when they're now much more incubus-like than before. Daeva, as a whole, embody the sexuality aspects of Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T06:38:31-07:00","id":936059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christoph+</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/866135-how-addicting-is-the-\u200bkiss-of-the-succubus?p=936012#post936012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting, how would a blood bond 3, vitae adiction and an addiction caused by the Kiss of Succubus combined together feel like?<br /> <br /> How would this be perceived by the thrall?<br /> <br /> It would probably make it even harder to think about something else than the regnant ....</div> </div> </div> </div>The blood bond makes the thrall obsessed with the regnant. The Kiss of the Succubus makes the thrall experience withdrawl symptoms if they don't get bitten by the regnant periodically. The Vitae addiction makes them experience withdrawl symptoms if they don't drink Vitae (from any vampire) periodically, and makes it extremely difficult for them to resist an opportunity to drink Vitae (again, from any vampire) any time one is available.<br /> <br /> Those are the symptoms. How a character deals with those symptoms is dependent on the individual person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}